 "reading": "R_T with wrong-scene BEV does NOT beat R_none: it is far worse than R_none (-9.3 pts PDMS, +4.9 pp NC+TTC, +5.3 pp DAC) and worse than applying no correction at all (-3.4 pts vs original drafts, DAC 9.9% vs 8.0%). R_T output is driven by the scene-specific content of the BEV; the R_T - R_none advantage is not an extra-channel/capacity effect. Same pattern in every stratum incl. the 10 drive-held-out logs. Limit: a cross-scene shuffle is out-of-distribution (BEV road layout contradicts the drafts), so it shows R_T relies on the BEV being of the right scene, not WHICH part (teacher object knowledge vs road layout vs place memory) carries the advantage; it does not address the drive-overlap threat (navtest does)."
}